@page "/work"
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="dot"></span>Selected work</span>
        <h1 class="page-title reveal reveal-d1">Case studies.</h1>
        <p class="page-sub reveal reveal-d2">
            Proof, not promises. Every engagement starts with a real business constraint, moves
            through focused engineering, and ends with a measurable result.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container cases-list">

        <!-- CS 01 -->
        <article class="case-study reveal">
            <div class="cs-media">
                <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/1837726/pexels-photo-1837726.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
                     alt="Modern library interior with open staircases and bookshelves" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="cs-meta">
                <span class="case-tag">Government · Education · Singapore &amp; China</span>
                <span class="cs-index">01</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="display-2 cs-title">Rebuilding a government library portal in Blazor</h2>
            <div class="cs-tags">
                <span class="tag">.NET Blazor</span><span class="tag">Syncfusion</span>
                <span class="tag">WCAG 2.0</span><span class="tag">HTML/CSS</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-grid">
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Challenge</div>
                    <p>A government-style library portal needed to be recreated in Blazor while
                        preserving the polish and usability of an existing React and MUI-based
                        interface - and become a flexible white-label solution that could be
                        customized for multiple institutions across China and Singapore.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Approach</div>
                    <p>We rebuilt the experience in .NET Blazor, translating the React interface
                        into a reusable component architecture that supports institution-specific
                        branding, layouts, and workflows - with accessibility-conscious patterns for
                        high-traffic catalogue browsing and search.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Outcome</div>
                    <div class="cs-outcome">100<span>%</span></div>
                    <p>A reusable foundation for delivering branded library portal experiences
                        faster, while cutting the effort needed to maintain separate frontends per
                        institution.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- CS 02 -->
        <article class="case-study reveal reveal-d1">
            <div class="cs-media">
                <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/28606651/pexels-photo-28606651.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
                     alt="Modern residential building in the Netherlands" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="cs-meta">
                <span class="case-tag">PropTech · Netherlands</span>
                <span class="cs-index">02</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="display-2 cs-title">Reducing rental check-in time by 60% with custom .NET</h2>
            <div class="cs-tags">
                <span class="tag">.NET Core</span><span class="tag">Biometric / TOTP 2FA</span>
                <span class="tag">Azure Functions</span><span class="tag">Digital Signatures</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-grid">
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Challenge</div>
                    <p>A rental management operation in the Netherlands was slowed by manual
                        onboarding and paper-based documentation. Property managers spent too much
                        time on check-ins, and tenants experienced unnecessary delays.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Approach</div>
                    <p>We designed and deployed a full-stack .NET system to digitize the rental
                        workflow end to end - secure authentication, digital signatures, automated
                        PDF generation, and a mobile-responsive booking experience, deployed on IIS
                        for real operational use.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Outcome</div>
                    <div class="cs-outcome">60<span>%</span></div>
                    <p>Check-in processing time dropped by 60%. Paper handoffs were replaced with
                        secure, auditable records, and the mobile-first flow moved tenants from
                        interest to confirmation faster.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- CS 03 -->
        <article class="case-study reveal reveal-d2">
            <div class="cs-media">
                <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/3855771/pexels-photo-3855771.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
                     alt="Mechanic working in an automotive repair shop" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="cs-meta">
                <span class="case-tag">Automotive · Business Operations</span>
                <span class="cs-index">03</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="display-2 cs-title">Modernizing a legacy invoicing system from WPF to Blazor</h2>
            <div class="cs-tags">
                <span class="tag">Blazor WASM PWA</span><span class="tag">WPF Migration</span>
                <span class="tag">Docotic PDF</span><span class="tag">Azure DevOps</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-grid">
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Challenge</div>
                    <p>An automotive repair business ran on a legacy invoicing workflow that
                        limited scalability and slowed internal processes. The system needed to
                        move to a modern web architecture without losing the workflows staff
                        already depended on.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Approach</div>
                    <p>We migrated key functionality from WPF to .NET Blazor, preserving familiar
                        productivity patterns with Excel-like keyboard interactions inside data
                        grids, and engineered a high-performance PDF pipeline using Docotic for
                        consistent document rendering.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="cs-label">Outcome</div>
                    <div class="cs-outcome">Web<span>-based</span></div>
                    <p>A more modern, scalable invoicing platform with faster workflows and
                        stronger long-term maintainability - while keeping the operational
                        familiarity staff needed to stay productive.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt section-border-t work-cta">
    <div class="container cta-row">
        <p class="display-2" style="max-width:520px;">Build the kind of system your business can grow on.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a conversation →</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("GSTApp.initReveal");
    }
}
